# 14. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

These rules must be reflected in the interface and frontend behaviour.

1. A homeowner can belong to a project and a contractor can manage multiple projects.
2. Multiple expenses can be recorded for one project.
3. One purchase can have multiple delivery records.
4. One purchase or expense can have multiple partial payments.
5. Expenses and payments must remain separate records.
6. Uploading a receipt does not automatically mean that a payment has been made.
7. Homeowner acknowledgement does not mean professional verification.
8. Disputed records must remain visible with their dispute history.
9. Important financial edits should have an audit-history interface.
10. Users should only see and perform actions permitted by their role.
11. The system must not automatically approve records because a homeowner has not responded.
12. Progress updates must be identified as contractor-reported information.

